{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475766-fetish-idea-need-feeback","id":1475766,"title":"fetish idea - need feeback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-03T23:05:25-08:00","id":1475766,"title":"fetish idea - need feeback","content":"I am considering a new Fetish to add to my chronicle. The general idea is that when activated, it makes one's footprints in lupus appear like an appropriate animal that won't attract attention, like a dog (but possibly others, like coyotes or some other common canine local to the area).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Gnosis 6 to roll to activate, and that it'd be a level two Fetish. Once activated it'd be good for a scene (which is sufficiently vague that it could be a while).<br /> <br /> The basic idea is to have something that makes preserving the Veil easier as PCs like to wander about in lupus or hispo, and I as the ST don't want to bother with the consequences of someone leaving wolf tracks all over the place when there shouldn't be wolves in the area. I figure it's a win/win if I can provide something to the PCs that let's them do what they want and enables me to avoid issues concerning the Veil. I figure in the setting, this would be one of the more common fetishes for urban Garou and even rural Garou in areas where there aren't wolves.<br /> <br /> Do the mechanics check out? Or do I need to do something else?<br /> <br /> While I have some flavor text description ideas in my head, also interested if anyone has their own ideas about this they would like to share. I might incorporate that into the official fetish description I give my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T23:59:20-08:00","id":1475767,"title":"","content":"I'd go with an amulet type of fetish, possibly with fur of other wild animals, as part of it.<br /> I think the mechanics are okay. If fetishes are rather common in your chronicle I would go with level one. Or, a level three fetish, that works for two Garou per success, if they travel together.<br /> <br /> You could tie the difficulty to the Gauntlet, making travelling in rural areas easier, but not sneaking into a pentex oil refinery...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T00:56:28-08:00","id":1475768,"title":"","content":"Considering how similar wolf and dog prints can be, unless larger dogs aren't common to an area, it would be extremely difficult to tell if tracks were from one or the other. Even most experts, if presented with wolf-like tracks in a place with no known wolves but a known dog population would err on the side of it being a dog instead of a wolf. A Garou that's aware of some of the clues of wolf vs.dog can also influence this by behavior or other context clues. Dogs tend to meander and investigate things more than wolves do, meaning wolves tend to move in straight lines while dogs tend to leave messier tracks... unless there's human tracks where wolves do not generally walk along side humans, and a well trained dog will fall into a neat line with a human handler.<br /> <br /> I think, given how much just learning how to &quot;walk&quot; like a dog in lupus could be done without a Fetish, I think this Fetish becomes a very niche item. Perhaps a more general &quot;turn your tracks into those of something else of your choosing,&quot; and the number of successes determining how different from your current form you can get, would be better. That would give them a bit more versatility beyond just making the Veil easier to keep (giving your Hispo tracks bear prints and messing around with some garbage cans/etc. vs. giving yourself the local large cat's prints would result in very different responses from the local humans beyond just not looking for a wolf).<br /> <br /> It might also be worth looking at the Air Foot Anklets from Hammer &amp; Klaive as a slightly different approach... and something already in the books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T15:36:48-08:00","id":1475947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475766-fetish-idea-need-feeback?p=1475767#post1475767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the mechanics are okay. If fetishes are rather common in your chronicle I would go with level one. Or, a level three fetish, that works for two Garou per success, if they travel together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say fetishes are common in my chronicles. I typically have it that on average Cliaths don't have any, a Fostern might have one level one or two fetish, and that at Adren and above a Garou typically has a number of fetish levels equal to their rank times two. That was my impression of how the Rage Across books gave them to NPCs, and I decided that worked for me. That's just an average, so some NPCs may have more or less. But when creating NPCs I try to keep to that standard.<br /> <br /> Having one fetish, probably for the pack leader, that could benefit the entire pack is an intriguing idea. It means I would need less fetishes which is a good thing. Of course I'd need to determine when a pack Garou no longer benefits from it. But using something like line of sight of the pack leader/fetish owner would probably work for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T22:55:22-08:00","id":1476080,"title":"","content":"I just saw a near identical fetish in Dark Ages: Werewolf - the Anklet of False Trails (page 221). It is a level one fetish (Gnosis 5) that disguises the trail of its wearer of whatever animal fur the anklet is made of.<br /> <br /> I still like the idea that a level two fetish might work on multiple Garou, but I now have a baseline of a fetish that works for one Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T23:14:11-08:00","id":1476081,"title":"","content":"Would also be nice, if a suitable Crafts roll would allow to exchange the fur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}